    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d196">

                <pb facs="0253" n="161" xml:id="pg161"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt
                    Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The President to the
                        Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d196-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">operational priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-08">8 November 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For Ambassador Harriman from the
                    President.</p>
                <p>My 041707,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d196-f2"/> your 06100.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d196-f3"/></p>
                <p>You are hereby authorized to attach our agreement regarding Turkey to the
                    protocol with the following change.</p>
                <p>Change the words “Commanders responsible” to the words “Combined Chiefs of
                        Staff.”<anchor n="4" xml:id="d196-f4"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Roosevelt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d196-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d196-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the United States Naval Attaché, Moscow, via Navy channels. A copy was
                    sent to the Department of State for its information.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d196-f2" n="2" xml:id="d196-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram of November 4, 1943; see <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg151">p. 151</ref>, footnote 1.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d196-f3" n="3" xml:id="d196-f3-content">
                <p>Telegram of November 6, 1943, <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg158">p. 158</ref>. The date-time group was garbled.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d196-f4" n="4" xml:id="d196-f4-content">
                <p>See Churchill’s telegram 493, November 6,
                    1943, to Roosevelt, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg156">p. 156</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
